[statement]
A name packages only provide, none of whose candidates apk would choose
for it, is decided after every other name: `c`, requested and walked
before `v`, has one candidate, `f`, which provides it at no version and
without a priority; `v` takes `f`, which then answers `c`, and apk
installs `f` alone. With nothing else to install `f`, apk refuses `c`
(`providers/a-name-provided-at-no-version-needs-a-priority`).

[repository]
P:f
V:1
p:v=1 c

[request]
c
v

[answer apk-tools 3.0.9-r0]
install f 1
